WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.070 line:80%
A 24-hour competition is
not one job: preparation,

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.460 line:80%
deployment and live
operations all run at once.

00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:14.394 line:80%
The event ran for a full day, and
the three overlapped from the first hour.

00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:21.268 line:80%
The public archive keeps
the challenges separate:

00:00:21.278 --> 00:00:25.628 line:80%
web services and an Android
reverse-engineering exercise,

00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:28.448 line:80%
each with its own source and dependencies.

00:00:29.309 --> 00:00:32.409 line:80%
Dockerfiles package the web applications,

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:35.839 line:80%
and Compose describes how
a service is built and exposed,

00:00:35.849 --> 00:00:38.409 line:80%
so a deployment can be repeated.

00:00:39.269 --> 00:00:42.339 line:80%
Once it started, the work moved
to monitoring,

00:00:42.349 --> 00:00:44.579 line:80%
troubleshooting and participant support.

00:00:47.632 --> 00:00:51.942 line:80%
The event’s internals stay out
of this film: no participant data,

00:00:51.952 --> 00:00:57.202 line:80%
no live infrastructure, and roles only
as the case study documents them.

00:00:58.148 --> 00:01:03.228 line:80%
Infrastructure and challenge development
met in one loop: environments prepared,

00:01:03.238 --> 00:01:06.478 line:80%
services deployed, participants supported.
